/*****************************************************************************
    kant8M1 -- M1, THE RETURN-CHANNEL PROBE. Jitted arm. 2026-08-10.

    Asks two questions that ladder rung JRt3 cannot answer, on one action so
    there is exactly one testing call and the sequential-state tar baby is
    unconstructable in this fixture's shape.

    ONE. Which channel does a returned local traverse on each engine. The
    interpreted arm is expected to hand back the node itself, which the frame
    sweep has already reverted under the caller. The jitted arm is expected to
    hand back a value that left the node before the sweep could reach it.

    TWO, and this is the one nothing in the tree measures. The frame the jit
    builds is scoped to integer counts. A local holding text has no slot in it.
    So a text local and a count local may sit on opposite sides of the same
    fence, and which side each lands on is the floor the parse templates will
    be built on.

    The action prints both locals from INSIDE, before and after the nested
    call, because reading a local from outside afterwards would mean reading
    the very quantity under test across the boundary being measured. It
    returns the count local, so the returned value is a third reading rather
    than a repeat of the second.

    Its interpreted twin lives in kant8M1o and runs in its own process, for
    the reason recorded on jitJRt2o. A post-jit interpreted call is not a
    clean oracle for a returned value.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, exactly ONE stop.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(Kant8M1);
define
    m1n;
    m1out;
    m1 code={
        m1count = m1n + 40;
        m1text  = "alive";
        print "M1 jit  before  : m1count =" m1count " m1text =" m1text:;
        if m1n > 0;
            m1n = m1n - 1;
            m1();
        print "M1 jit  after   : m1count =" m1count " m1text =" m1text:;
        return m1count;
        };
    ;

m1n = 2;
print "M1 jit  fire 1 setup : m1n =" m1n:;
testing(m1);

m1n = 5;
print "M1 jit  fire 2 setup : m1n =" m1n " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();

print "M1 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
